Integrating DevSecOps into Security Programs
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the fundamental concepts of DevSecOps and its role in modern software development • Set up a basic DevSecOps pipeline using open-source tools • Implement security scanning tools in a CI/CD pipeline • Configure automated security testing for code vulnerabilities • Integrate security monitoring and logging into development workflows • Analyze security scan results and implement remediation strategies • Establish security gates in the development pipeline

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) • Familiarity with Linux command line operations • Basic knowledge of Git version control • Understanding of containerization concepts (Docker basics) • Awareness of cybersecurity fundamentals

